  "body": "WebKit and Blink enforce a maximal depth of backtracking of 1,000,000 (see [here](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/d42ba8c64e46430dacf3c77d4e3ae1ea840d44c4/Source/JavaScriptCore/yarr/Yarr.h#L50C48-L50C48) for WebKit, [here](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=966405) for Blink) when checking an input's value against a regular expression specified in [#the-pattern-attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-input-pattern). Gecko is discussing this in [Bug 1837772](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1837772). Without such a limit, a pattern like `(\\d+)*` can hang a tab.\r\n\r\nSuch a backtracking limit could be included in the spec around the pattern attribute and it might be worth to discuss whether this limit should also be applied in other situations. There is already [this](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/forms/constraints/infinite_backtracking.html) wpt testing this behavior.",
